&lt;p&gt;DoorDash for Business is building the premier corporate dining and benefits platform—helping companies of all sizes feed their teams through industry-leading products and meal programs. Our mission is to become the go-to solution for executives, administrators, and employees who need seamless, high-quality food programs at work. We move fast, operate with an ownership mindset, and are growing new product lines to better serve our corporate customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Associate Manager on the DoorDash for Business Catering team, you will own the Dasher and delivery experience for catering—making sure large, high-stakes catering orders show up on time, get handed off and set up correctly, and reach the customer the way they expect.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work at the intersection of operations, logistics, and analytics—getting deep into the details of how catering deliveries actually play out on the ground, forming hypotheses about what&#39;s breaking, and running small, fast tests to find what works before we scale it. This is early-stage, hands-on problem solving, not optimizing a machine that already runs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Senior Manager, Strategy &amp;amp; Operations for DoorDash for Business and can work remotely or hybrid depending preference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Dasher quality for catering: Take end-to-end ownership of delivery quality for catering—on-time arrival, accurate drop-off and setup, and a clean handoff—so customers can trust every order.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build net new logistics: Figure out how catering and deliveries should actually work—Dasher selection, batching, timing, equipment, and handoff—by testing different approaches and learning what holds up in the real world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get into the details: Dig into individual deliveries, talk to Dashers and customers, and trace exactly where things break down—then turn those root causes into concrete operational fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to optimize how we operate&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Build the automated workflows that show where catering deliveries break down—and lean on AI to turn slow, manual analysis and one-off fixes into repeatable processes the team can scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the Product Roadmap: Translate what you learn on the ground into clear product and operational recommendations that make catering delivery more reliable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re excited about you because…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 4–6 years of experience in strategy &amp;amp; operations, logistics, management consulting, or a high-growth marketplace environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of owning cross-functional operational problems end-to-end—from diagnosis to testing to rollout—and are comfortable building from scratch in ambiguous, early-stage environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience owning partner-team relationships and working closely with Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re analytically strong: you write SQL, work fluently with data, and know how to get to the root cause and turn complexity into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate fluency with AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Cursor, or similar) to automate workflows, surface insights, and drive faster, better decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate with clarity and influence—you can tailor your message for Dashers, operators, cross-functional partners, and senior leadership alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love getting into the weeds—you&#39;ll happily roll up your sleeves, get to the lowest level of detail, and run the test yourself to find out what works.&lt;/li&gt;
