&lt;p&gt;Design Program Managers make DoorDash&#39;s Design Studio run better. As owner of the Logistics pillar within Design Operations, you&#39;re accountable for one of our most important operating outcomes: maximizing the bandwidth of the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll find where ICs and managers lose time, fragmented workflows, manual processes, meeting overload, unclear rhythms, and you&#39;ll define and build the tools and systems that fix it. That might mean shipping a new internal tool, automating a recurring workflow, redesigning how scheduling or reviews work, or establishing a better operating cadence. You own the full loop: diagnose the problem, design the system, build the tool, measure whether it worked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Logistics outcome, maximize the bandwidth of the team. ICs and managers have more usable time. Meeting load decreases. The team can focus on high-value work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the biggest sources of operational drag across the Studio and turn them into a prioritized roadmap of tools and process fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and build the tools, automations, and workflows that reduce manual coordination, including for scheduling, budgets, vendor management, and event logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redesign how the Studio operates: reviews, planning cadences, rhythms for both ICs and managers, information flows,&amp;nbsp; whatever determines how fast teams can move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure whether your systems work, usable time for ICs and managers, meeting load, adoption, hours of manual work eliminated, and iterate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn recurring requests into scalable solutions. The second time a problem shows up, build the thing that stops a third.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own scheduling, budget, vendor, and logistics programs as a builder, not a permanent executor, your job is to make them need less manual effort every quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with (and, as scope grows, help develop) other DPMs on the Logistics pod.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re excited about you because you have…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in operations, program management, or business operations, building systems and tools that made a complex org run better. Design/product/creative org experience is a plus; EA or Chief of Staff backgrounds are welcome if you&#39;ve built beyond pure execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder mindset: you&#39;ve created tools, workflows, or automations that replaced manual work — not just performed manual work well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product-manager instincts applied to operations: find the real pain point, diagnose root cause, prototype, ship, measure, iterate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to own an outcome independently at L4/L5 scope — you don&#39;t need the problem pre-scoped for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with AI and no-code tooling (Claude, Cursor, Figma, or similar) to prototype and ship internal tools without needing an engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written/verbal communication and the judgment to handle sensitive leadership and operational info with discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What success looks like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maximize the bandwidth of the team. ICs and managers have more usable time. Meeting load decreases. Team can focus on high-value work. Manual workflows become automated. Recurring problems become systems that scale. Your job is to create capacity — not just manage it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
