&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash Labs is a team within DoorDash building autonomous delivery robots and other autonomy solutions from the ground up for DoorDash&#39;s core delivery platform. If you have a passion for applying autonomy and robotics in a service used by millions of people daily, then we want to talk to you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a hands-on&lt;strong&gt; Electrical Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to review the design, drawings, and schematics of the electrical systems for our 4-wheeled autonomous delivery robot. This role is responsible for delivering robust, production-ready hardware across high-speed digital design, PCBAs, RF integration, harnessing, and board-level packaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a deeply technical position for someone who can move seamlessly between system-level thinking and detailed circuit execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re excited about this opportunity because...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop electrical systems for a complex mobile robotic platform from concept through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-speed digital design efforts (PCIe, MIPI, Ethernet, DDR, multi-gigabit SERDES, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own PCBA development including schematic capture, stack-up definition, layout guidance, impedance control, and design-for-manufacture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive RF integration (Wi-Fi, LTE/5G, GNSS, Bluetooth, RADAR, and LiDAR), antenna placement, layout constraints, and signal integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and review cable harness designs, connector selection, grounding strategy, and environmental robustness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with mechanical engineering on board packaging, thermal management, vibration resistance, and environmental sealing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement power distribution architecture, battery interfaces, protection circuits, and system monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with EMI/EMC and regulatory requirements (FCC/CE) (CISPR-25 and FCC Part 15 Class A).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prototype builds and bring-up, debug hardware/firmware interface issues, root-cause failures, and drive corrective actions quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish design standards and perform detailed design reviews across the EE team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with firmware, robotics, systems, manufacturing, and reliability teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re excited about you because...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or M.S. in Electrical Engineering (or equivalent experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-7+ years of experience designing complex embedded hardware systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-speed digital circuit design and layout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-layer PCB design and stack-up planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Signal integrity and power integrity fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RF integration and antenna considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cable harness and interconnect design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMI/EMC mitigation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing EMC/EMI input and output filters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking hardware products from concept to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile or ruggedized systems operating in real-world environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and lab bring-up experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(VNA and Spectrum Analyzer experience is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in robotics, automotive, aerospace, or industrial automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with safety-critical or high-reliability systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-voltage battery systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with environmental, vibration, and regulatory testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with contract manufacturers and NPI processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on engineer who enjoys building and shipping real hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems intuition with attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in fast-moving, cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic decision-maker balancing performance, cost, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator and technical mentor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
