&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Hardware Systems Engineer to own system-level architecture across electrical, mechanical, firmware, sensor, and compute subsystems – decomposing platform requirements into verifiable specs for power distribution, motion control, embedded compute, sensor suites and communication buses (CAN, Ethernet, etc.). You&#39;ll drive requirements traceability, interface control documents (ICDs), trade studies, and verification and validation (V&amp;amp;V) plans that ensure subsystems built by separate EE, ME, firmware, and perception teams function as one safe, reliable delivery robot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own system-level architecture across electrical, mechanical, firmware, sensor, and compute subsystems for autonomous delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decompose platform requirements into verifiable specs for power distribution, motion control, embedded compute, and sensor suites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive requirements traceability, ICDs, trade studies, and V&amp;amp;V plans across EE, ME, firmware, and perception workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define fault-tolerant architectures (FMEA, fault trees, redundancy) governing system behavior during component failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional root-cause debugging across hardware, firmware, and software boundaries, conducting design and safety reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business and regulatory requirements into engineering specs in collaboration with Product, Safety, Legal, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re excited about you because…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in EE, ME, Computer Science, Systems Engineering, Robotics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience building, testing, and validating mechatronics or sensor-equipped hardware in robotics, automotive, or aerospace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in embedded systems architecture, vehicle mechanicals, electronics, and autonomous perception systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to perform cross-boundary debugging across hardware, firmware, and software layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate complex trade-offs, identify failure modes, and translate ambiguous business and regulatory goals into precise, verifiable engineering specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leading complex, multi-disciplinary projects across EE, ME, firmware, and perception teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate’s starting pay will fall within the pay range listed below and is determined based on job-related factors including, but not limited to, skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. Base salary is localized according to an employee’s work location. Ranges are market-dependent and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, the compensation for this role includes opportunities for equity grants. Talk to your recruiter for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
