&lt;p&gt;DoorDash Labs is an independent robotics and automation team within DoorDash, focused on transforming last-mile logistics at scale. Our work reaches millions of people — and we&#39;re building the operational foundation to make that possible safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Safety, Robot Operations&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead the safety vision for one of the &lt;strong&gt;world&#39;s most advanced autonomous delivery operations&lt;/strong&gt;. You will continue to&amp;nbsp; build on world-class safety culture across our fleet, depots, field operations—ensuring that safety is embedded into each process robot deployment, service management, under the roof and out on road operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic leadership role responsible for operating mechanisms, governance, audits, standards, and continuous improvement systems that enable safe, scalable, and compliant autonomous robot operations. You will partner closely with Operations, Engineering, Product, Hardware, Reliability, and Legal to proactively identify risks, prevent incidents, and continuously raise the safety bar as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture: &lt;/strong&gt;Safety is the foundational pillar of our operations. You will continue to sharpen the strong safety-first culture where every operator is empowered and accountable for safe operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and execute the long-term safety strategy for Dot Operations. Develop safety management systems, policies, standards, SOPs, and governance mechanisms. Partner with Engineering and Product teams to identify operational safety risks and influence safer robot, hardware, and software designs. Engage with regulators, represent DoorDash externally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day to Day Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead incident investigations, root cause analyses, corrective actions, and lessons-learned programs to eliminate repeat events. Develop leading safety metrics, dashboards, KPIs, and own executive reporting mechanisms. Lead emergency response, crisis management, and business continuity preparedness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Strengthen comprehensive audit programs to evaluate operational safety, process compliance, and facility readiness. Own operational risk assessments for new products, launches, depots, and markets. Develop and execute &lt;strong&gt;simulated SEV0 incident exercises&lt;/strong&gt; to validate response playbooks, decision-making, communication protocols, escalation paths, and recovery mechanisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and mentor a high-performing safety organization capable of supporting rapid global scale. Stregthene training and certification programs for operators, technicians, and frontline leaders. Drive continuous improvement initiatives that improve both safety performance and operational efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience leading safety programs within technology harnessed operations like logistics, robotics, automotive, autonomous systems, aviation, warehouse or other high-reliability environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building enterprise-scale safety management systems from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of operational risk management, hazard identification, incident investigation, and preventive controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading safety audits, compliance reviews, and operational governance programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence senior executives and cross-functional engineering and operations organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with experience using data to identify trends, predict risk, and improve safety outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and leadership skills with the ability to build trust across all organizational levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering, Safety, Industrial Engineering, Operations, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a high speed, ambiguous, dusty, technology environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in autonomous vehicles, robotics, industrial automation, or advanced mobility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as CSP, CIH, CHST, Six Sigma, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing ISO-based safety management systems (e.g., ISO 45001) or comparable operational excellence frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling safety programs across multiple sites or international operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with human factors engineering, safety-by-design principles, and high-reliability organization (HRO) practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in Engineering, Safety, Operations, or Business.&lt;/li&gt;
