&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash Labs is an independent team within DoorDash. We are working on building autonomous delivery robots from the ground up and other automation solutions as part of DoorDash&#39;s core delivery platform. If you have a passion for applying AI and robotics solutions in a service used by millions of people, then we want to talk to you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note:&lt;/strong&gt; This role is based in San Francisco, CA, and requires being in-person 5 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a master-level&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Prototype Machinist &amp;amp; Fabrication Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Prototype Integration (PI) Team. This is a high-impact role designed for a &quot;maker&quot; with a deep technical pedigree in both traditional and cutting-edge manufacturing. You will be the primary resource for the engineering team, responsible for transforming complex designs into high-precision physical hardware. You are an expert in 5-axis CNC machining, CNC lathes, and manual machining, as well as a power user of a diverse 3D printing fleet. When not machining, you will serve as a Prototype and Integration Technician, helping the team assemble and troubleshoot the robotic platforms you helped create.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and program 5-axis CNC machines, CNC lathes, and manual mills/lathes to produce high-tolerance prototype components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the daily operation, post-processing, and maintenance of 3D printing technologies including FDM, SLS, and SLA platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and fabricate custom jigs, fixtures, and specialized tooling to support complex assemblies and unique testing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret engineering drawings, blueprints, and CAD models to ensure all builds meet exact specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback to Mechanical Engineers on Design for Manufacturability (DFM) to optimize part production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventative maintenance on all shop machinery and shop-specific equipment to ensure zero downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inventory for machinist-specific consumables including cutting tools, inserts, coolants, resins, and filaments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the physical assembly, wiring, and mechanical troubleshooting of robotic delivery vehicles and test fixtures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, organized, and OSHA-compliant machine shop environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead EH&amp;amp;S efforts within the shop, including PPE compliance and hazardous material (MSDS) management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use computers for documentation, record-keeping, and tracking of calibration schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with the engineering team to prioritize high-urgency prototype requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re excited about you because you have…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 7+ years of experience in a high-precision machine shop, R&amp;amp;D lab, or prototype environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of 5-axis CNC programming and operation, CNC lathes, and manual machining equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in the use of precision measurement tools such as micrometers, calipers, bore gauges, and CMM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing professional-grade 3D printing platforms (e.g., Formlabs, Markforged, Carbon).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong manual dexterity and hand-eye coordination required for precision assembly and tool operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull materials and equipment weighing up to 50 pounds on a regular basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to work in physically demanding environments, including standing for extended periods and working around machinery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High visual acuity to read blueprints, measure accurately, and perform detailed craftsmanship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CAD/CAM software (Mastercam, HSMWorks, Fusion 360, SolidWorks, or Onshape) for toolpath generation and model navigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to wear and work safely with required Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) including eye and ear protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred experience includes…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced fabrication skills such as TIG/MIG welding or sheet metal fabrication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the robotics, aerospace, or automotive industry working on autonomous systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in electronics including reading schematics and performing basic soldering or wire harness fabrication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Linux or Python for basic robotic system testing and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid U.S. driver’s license&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
