&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash’s growing Accounting team supports a rapidly evolving marketplace business and offers opportunities to build new processes and develop your career. We’re looking for a Revenue Accounting Manager to strengthen our revenue accounting operations and help our processes scale with the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Senior Revenue Accounting Manager on our Revenue Accounting team and lead a small team of full-time accountants and outsourced or contract resources. You will own assigned revenue accounting areas, lead the related close activities, and partner across teams to support new products and improve accounting processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly close for assigned revenue accounting areas, overseeing journal entries, account reconciliations, variance analysis, and management reporting to deliver complete, accurate, and timely financial results in accordance with U.S. GAAP and internal policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance SOX controls for assigned revenue processes, ensure supporting documentation is complete, and coordinate responses to internal and external audit requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop the team, set priorities, review deliverables, and resolve close issues, escalating significant accounting judgments, risks, or delays to the Senior Revenue Accounting Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Technical Accounting, Finance, Legal, Data &amp;amp; Engineering, Sales Operations, Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, and business owners to implement accounting requirements and drive improvements to policies, processes, and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead process improvements and automation initiatives, including applying AI tools to tasks such as manual journal entries, reconciliations and variance analysis, to reduce manual work and improve the accuracy and efficiency of monthly and quarterly closes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate discrepancies in automated and scripted revenue entries, partnering with Revenue Data to identify root causes, drive corrections, and prevent recurrence across transaction data flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document accounting processes for new products, create and maintain standard operating procedures, and update documentation as processes and systems change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the accounting and revenue recognition implications of new products, features, and platform tests; draft initial accounting considerations and partner with Technical Accounting to resolve key judgments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Revenue Data and Engineering to review test transactions and source data in Snowflake, validate accounting entries before launch, and automate the related accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re excited about you because…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of progressive accounting experience, including revenue accounting and experience with accounting operations and financial systems; a combination of Big 4 public accounting and corporate experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience directly managing and developing an accounting team; experience overseeing outsourced or contract resources preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of U.S. GAAP, ASC 606 revenue recognition, and SOX/internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate to advanced Excel skills and experience analyzing large volumes of transactional data; familiarity with ERP or revenue systems preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL experience preferred, with a willingness to develop and apply SQL skills to accounting investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in applying AI and automation tools to improve accounting efficiency and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, sound judgment, and the ability to adapt to changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain accounting requirements and data issues to non-accounting partners and all levels of management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate’s starting pay will fall within the pay range listed below and is determined based on job-related factors including, but not limited to, skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. Base salary is localized according to an employee’s work location. Ranges are market-dependent and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, the compensation for this role includes opportunities for equity grants. Talk to your recruiter for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash cares about you and your overall well-being. That’s why we offer a comprehensive benefits package to all regular employees, which includes a 401(k) plan with employer matching, 16 weeks of paid parental leave, wellness benefits, commuter benefits match, paid time off and paid sick leave in compliance with applicable laws (e.g. Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act). DoorDash also offers medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, disability and basic life insurance, family-forming assistance, and a mental health program, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our benefits, visit our careers page &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doordash.com/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See below for paid time off details:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For salaried roles:&lt;/strong&gt; flexible paid time off/vacation, plus 80 hours of paid sick time per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For hourly roles:&lt;/strong&gt; vacation accrued at about 1 hour for every 25.97 hours worked (e.g. about 6.7 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 3.4 hours/month if working 20 hours/week), and paid sick time accrued at 1 hour for every 30 hours worked (e.g. about 5.8 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 2.9 hours/month if working 20 hours/week).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The national base pay range for this position within the United States, including Illinois and Colorado.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$124,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$183,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks including premium healthcare, wellness expense reimbursement, paid parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/p&gt;
