&lt;p&gt;DoorDash Labs is DoorDash&#39;s autonomous delivery group, building the robots and hardware that move goods without a driver. The Hardware team designs the electronics at the core of these systems — digital and mixed-signal control boards, power and motor-control electronics, embedded firmware, and the test and integration benches that prove the whole system works. We&#39;re building out an experienced and diverse set of electrical engineers to increase our velocity, bandwidth, and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own mixed-signal and analog design — a key capability gap for the team — and raise the analog bar across our control hardware, from instrumentation and telemetry to sensor interfaces and precision analog. You will report into the Director, Electrical Engineering on our Hardware team in our DoorDash Labs organization. Our offices are open, and depending on the role this position is hybrid or fully onsite — expect to be fully onsite when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design instrumentation and telemetry-measurement circuits, precision current sources, and high-quality amplifiers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design circuits around ADCs, DACs, and signal conditioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design sensor interfaces — temperature, light, audio — and LED drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own power sequencing and EMC-aware analog design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring analog rigor to design reviews and help set analog/EMC design practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re excited about you because…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mixed-signal and precision-analog design background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrumentation, telemetry, current-source, and power-amplifier design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ADC/DAC and signal-conditioning design; sensor front-ends (temp/light/audio) and LED drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EMC/EMI-aware design and mitigation experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You characterize analog performance in the lab (noise, bandwidth, accuracy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate’s starting pay will fall within the pay range listed below and is determined based on job-related factors including, but not limited to, skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. Base salary is localized according to an employee’s work location. Ranges are market-dependent and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, the compensation for this role includes opportunities for equity grants. Talk to your recruiter for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
