&lt;p&gt;Notice to Applicants for Jobs Located in NYC or Remote Jobs Associated With Office in NYC Only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used Covey as part of our hiring and/or promotional process for jobs in NYC and certain features may qualify it as an AEDT in NYC. As part of the hiring and/or promotion process, we provided Covey with job requirements and candidate submitted applications. We began using Covey Scout for Inbound from August 21, 2023, through December 21, 2023.&amp;nbsp; We resumed using Covey Scout for Inbound again on June 29, 2024, and ceased using Covey Scout for Inbound on April 30, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Covey tool has been reviewed by an independent auditor. Results of the audit may be viewed here:&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&quot;&gt;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;UAS Operations Ground Support Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll join Flight Operations in a &lt;strong&gt;qualified Commercial Ground Support position &lt;/strong&gt;supporting safe, &lt;strong&gt;compliant UAS delivery operations under Part 135&lt;/strong&gt;. All hires complete &lt;strong&gt;required training and qualification under the company’s FAA-approved training program&lt;/strong&gt; before independently performing assigned duties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work alongside Remote Pilots in Command (RPICs), Flight Operations leadership, and Maintenance to &lt;strong&gt;support aircraft readiness, safe ground operations, and mission execution&lt;/strong&gt; through disciplined procedures and clear communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also work cross-functionally with Flight Test, Engineering, and other teams to &lt;strong&gt;support Part 107 testing&lt;/strong&gt;, developmental operations, and system validation within applicable authorizations and established safety controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as &lt;strong&gt;qualified Commercial Ground Support&lt;/strong&gt; within Flight Operations &lt;strong&gt;for Part 135 UAS operations&lt;/strong&gt; once trained, qualified, and authorized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complete training delivered by a qualified Ground Instructor under the company’s FAA-approved training program&lt;/strong&gt; and required competency evaluations. Initial-cadre members complete the applicable &lt;strong&gt;FAA qualification and evaluation process.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain &lt;strong&gt;required qualifications, recurrent training,&lt;/strong&gt; proficiency, and standardization requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support aircraft preparation&lt;/strong&gt;, staging, payload handling, battery management, equipment setup, launch and recovery, and aircraft turnaround &lt;strong&gt;within assigned responsibilities.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verify&lt;/strong&gt; aircraft, payload, equipment, and &lt;strong&gt;operating-area readiness in accordance with assigned Ground Support procedures and checklists.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply applicable Part 135 requirements, company manuals, SOPs, checklists, Operations Specifications, exemptions, waivers, and operating limitations&lt;/strong&gt; relevant to assigned duties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate with the RPIC&lt;/strong&gt; and operational personnel throughout missions, &lt;strong&gt;maintaining situational awareness and timely communication&lt;/strong&gt; of ground conditions and aircraft readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pause unsafe ground activities and promptly escalate concerns through established channels&lt;/strong&gt;. Flight command authority remains with the RPIC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify and report hazards&lt;/strong&gt;,&lt;strong&gt; aircraft discrepancies, equipment damage, and procedural deviations&lt;/strong&gt; through established safety and maintenance channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate training, qualification, operational, and equipment &lt;strong&gt;records required for assigned activities.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support abnormal and emergency operations within defined Ground Support responsibilities,&lt;/strong&gt; including required drills and emergency procedure training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work cross-functionally with Flight Test, Engineering, and other teams to support Part 107 testing&lt;/strong&gt;, developmental operations, demonstrations, and validation within assigned duties and applicable authorizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide structured operational feedback&lt;/strong&gt; and contribute to improvements in ground procedures, SOPs, checklists, equipment, and training materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When qualified and designated, qualify additional Ground Support crew members under the &lt;strong&gt;FAA-approved training program&lt;/strong&gt;. &lt;strong&gt;Training duties require separate qualification and designation as a Ground Instructor&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work outdoors with extended standing&lt;/strong&gt;, equipment handling, and &lt;strong&gt;varying weather conditions while following company safety practices and operating limits&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain schedule flexibility&lt;/strong&gt; for commercial operations, training, and testing, &lt;strong&gt;including day, evening, and weekend assignments as required&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Participate in the company’s FAA/DOT drug and alcohol testing program&lt;/strong&gt; when assigned duties are covered under 14 CFR Part 120, &lt;strong&gt;including pre-employment drug testing and applicable ongoing testing under 49 CFR Part 40&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You’re Excited About This Opportunity Because You Will…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold a qualified operational position&lt;/strong&gt; supporting commercial Part 135 UAS delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop through an FAA-approved training program&lt;/strong&gt; with defined qualification and proficiency standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work alongside pilots and Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt; to support aircraft readiness and safe mission execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with technical teams during Part 107 flight testing&lt;/strong&gt; and system validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be considered for additional qualification responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt; as your proficiency and program needs develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to safe, standardized, and scalable drone delivery operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re Excited About You Because…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have Relevant Operational Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Experience in UAS, aviation ground operations, logistics, maintenance, or another safety-critical environment is preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Meet and Maintain Qualification Standards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You hold a valid Part 107 certificate and you can complete required training, competency evaluations, recurrent training, and standardization requirements and maintain eligibility for assigned duties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Safety-Minded and Procedurally Disciplined:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You consistently follow manuals, SOPs, checklists, and operating limitations, recognize hazards, and pause or escalate activities when conditions are unsafe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Hands-On and Detail-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’re comfortable handling aircraft, batteries, payloads, and support equipment, and can identify incorrect configurations, discrepancies, and abnormal conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Communicate and Collaborate Clearly:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You provide timely, accurate operational callouts and work effectively with pilots, Maintenance, Flight Test, and cross-functional teams within defined responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Document with Discipline:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You maintain accurate training, qualification, operational, and equipment records and report observations clearly to support traceability, compliance, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Prepared for Additional Responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Additional qualification or Ground Instructor responsibilities require applicable training, evaluation, and company designation. Selection depends on demonstrated proficiency and program needs, with FAA approval where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications for this position are accepted on an ongoing basis&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within the pay range listed below will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, skills, prior relevant experience, and specific work location. Base salary is localized according to employee work location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash cares about you and your overall well-being. That’s why we offer a comprehensive benefits package to all regular employees, which includes a 401(k) plan with employer matching, 16 weeks of paid parental leave, wellness benefits, commuter benefits match, paid time off and paid sick leave in compliance with applicable laws (e.g. Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act). DoorDash also offers medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, disability and basic life insurance, family-forming assistance, and a mental health program, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our benefits, visit our careers page &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doordash.com/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See below for paid time off details:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For salaried roles:&lt;/strong&gt; flexible paid time off/vacation, plus 80 hours of paid sick time per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For hourly roles:&lt;/strong&gt; vacation accrued at about 1 hour for every 25.97 hours worked (e.g. about 6.7 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 3.4 hours/month if working 20 hours/week), and paid sick time accrued at 1 hour for every 30 hours worked (e.g. about 5.8 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 2.9 hours/month if working 20 hours/week).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The national base pay range for this position within the United States, including Illinois and Colorado.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$23.70&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$34.80 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks including premium healthcare, wellness expense reimbursement, paid parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Statement of Non-Discrimination: In keeping with our beliefs and goals, no employee or applicant will face discrimination or harassment based on: race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, age, gender, marital/domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability status, or veteran status. Above and beyond discrimination and harassment based on “protected categories,” we also strive to prevent other subtler forms of inappropriate behavior (i.e., stereotyping) from ever gaining a foothold in our office. Whether blatant or hidden, barriers to success have no place at DoorDash. We value a diverse workforce – people who identify as women, non-binary or gender non-conforming, LGBTQIA+, American Indian or Native Alaskan, Black or African American, Hispanic or Latinx, Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, differently-abled, caretakers and parents, and veterans are strongly encouraged to apply. Thank you to the Level Playing Field Institute for this statement of non-discrimination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and any other state or local hiring regulations, we will consider for employment any qualified applicant, including those with arrest and conviction records, in a manner consistent with the applicable regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you need any accommodations, please inform your recruiting contact upon initial connection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Applicants for Jobs Located in NYC or Remote Jobs Associated With Office in NYC Only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used Covey as part of our hiring and/or promotional process for jobs in NYC and certain features may qualify it as an AEDT in NYC. As part of the hiring and/or promotion process, we provided Covey with job requirements and candidate submitted applications. We began using Covey Scout for Inbound from August 21, 2023, through December 21, 2023.&amp;nbsp; We resumed using Covey Scout for Inbound again on June 29, 2024, and ceased using Covey Scout for Inbound on April 30, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Covey tool has been reviewed by an independent auditor. Results of the audit may be viewed here:&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&quot;&gt;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;UAS Operations Specialist -Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll support commercial drone delivery under Part 107 &amp;amp; 135 through scheduled and unscheduled fleet maintenance, inspection, and troubleshooting, while working alongside Flight Operations. All hires complete internal maintenance qualification, aircraft rating checks, and applicable pilot training to maintain operational readiness and safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based on technical expertise, aviation background, and fleet requirements, specialists can also be appointed as &lt;strong&gt;Maintenance Technicians&lt;/strong&gt;. These roles require formal company authorization along with &lt;strong&gt;FAA approval when mandated&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also perform aircraft rigging, component replacements, routine bench testing, and support &lt;strong&gt;Part 107 maintenance test flights and system validation&lt;/strong&gt; alongside &lt;strong&gt;Flight Test and Engineering teams&lt;/strong&gt; within FAA operating limitations and safety controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform &lt;strong&gt;scheduled and unscheduled aircraft maintenance, preventative maintenance, inspections, and repairs&lt;/strong&gt; across the commercial UAS fleet according to manufacturer procedures and Part 135 specs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and troubleshoot &lt;strong&gt;avionic, electrical, mechanical, and software system faults&lt;/strong&gt;, telemetry logs, and &lt;strong&gt;maintenance software.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain detailed &lt;strong&gt;aircraft logs, component history records, airworthiness tracking, and maintenance documentation&lt;/strong&gt; in compliance with company SOPs and FAA regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct &lt;strong&gt;preflight inspection, airworthiness verification, post-maintenance test flights, and ground engine/motor runs&lt;/strong&gt; prior to returning aircraft to active service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage &lt;strong&gt;spare parts inventory, tool control, Ground Support Equipment (GSE), and battery management systems&lt;/strong&gt; to support high-availability flight schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with &lt;strong&gt;Flight Test and Reliability Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to evaluate hardware failures, recommend design modifications, and refine maintenance procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with &lt;strong&gt;flight test personnel and cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; to execute approved test plans, flight test cards, procedures, and data collection objectives within the scope of assigned pilot duties to gain aircraft knowledge and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured feedback on &lt;strong&gt;aircraft behavior, system performance, pilot interfaces, procedures, and operational limitations&lt;/strong&gt; observed during commercial and test operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify hazards, aircraft discrepancies, abnormal conditions, and emerging risks through established channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in &lt;strong&gt;standardization and safety reporting&lt;/strong&gt;, and contribute operational expertise to SOPs, manuals, checklists, training materials, and flight procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;aircraft staging, equipment preparation, site setup, repositioning, and mission coordination&lt;/strong&gt; as needed to conduct flight operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in outdoor environments involving &lt;strong&gt;extended standing, equipment handling, and varying weather conditions&lt;/strong&gt;, while adhering to company safety practices and operating limits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain schedule flexibility for commercial operations, training, and testing, including day, evening, and weekend shifts as required by program needs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the company’s &lt;strong&gt;FAA/DOT drug and alcohol testing program&lt;/strong&gt;, including pre-employment drug screening and ongoing testing as required for assigned safety-sensitive duties under &lt;strong&gt;14 CFR Part 120 and 49 CFR Part 40&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You’re Excited About This Opportunity Because You Will…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine hands-on &lt;strong&gt;UAS maintenance and technical troubleshooting&lt;/strong&gt; with active drone piloting responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain airworthiness for a cutting-edge commercial fleet operating under &lt;strong&gt;FAA Part 107 &amp;amp; 135 regulations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply aviation fundamentals across &lt;strong&gt;commercial operations and Part 107 flight testing&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside &lt;strong&gt;flight test personnel and technical teams&lt;/strong&gt; to evaluate aircraft systems, procedures, and future capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to &lt;strong&gt;safe, scalable, and repeatable drone delivery operations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re Excited About You Because…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have Technical and Flight Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You hold an &lt;strong&gt;FAA Remote Pilot Certificate (Part 107)&lt;/strong&gt; and have practical experience in UAS assembly, maintenance, troubleshooting,&amp;nbsp; or equivalent technical background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re Skilled in Diagnostics &amp;amp; Rigging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are proficient with hand tools, multimeter testing, soldering, telemetry log analysis, and component-level repairs of complex electromechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Meet and Maintain Qualification Standards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can successfully complete required &lt;strong&gt;training, knowledge and competency evaluations, recurrent checks, and standardization requirements&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain eligibility for assigned maintenance duties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Procedurally Minded:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You consistently apply &lt;strong&gt;manuals, checklists, SOPs, operating limitations, and flight test procedures&lt;/strong&gt;, and exercise sound judgment when conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Can Support Flight Testing and Technical Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can execute defined test objectives, communicate observations clearly, and work effectively with &lt;strong&gt;Flight Test and cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; while maintaining pilot responsibilities and established safety controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Document with Discipline:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You maintain accurate &lt;strong&gt;flight, training, qualification, and operational records&lt;/strong&gt; and provide clear reporting that supports traceability, compliance, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be on the &lt;strong&gt;front lines of aerial innovation&lt;/strong&gt;, directly contributing to the development, validation, and scaling of commercial drone delivery systems. This is a &lt;strong&gt;high-impact, hands-on role&lt;/strong&gt; where your aviation judgment, technical skills, and procedural discipline help define how autonomous delivery operates in the real world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within the pay range listed below will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, skills, prior relevant experience, and specific work location. Base salary is localized according to employee work location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash cares about you and your overall well-being. That’s why we offer a comprehensive benefits package to all regular employees, which includes a 401(k) plan with employer matching, 16 weeks of paid parental leave, wellness benefits, commuter benefits match, paid time off and paid sick leave in compliance with applicable laws (e.g. Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act). DoorDash also offers medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, disability and basic life insurance, family-forming assistance, and a mental health program, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our benefits, visit our careers page &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doordash.com/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See below for paid time off details:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For salaried roles:&lt;/strong&gt; flexible paid time off/vacation, plus 80 hours of paid sick time per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For hourly roles:&lt;/strong&gt; vacation accrued at about 1 hour for every 25.97 hours worked (e.g. about 6.7 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 3.4 hours/month if working 20 hours/week), and paid sick time accrued at 1 hour for every 30 hours worked (e.g. about 5.8 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 2.9 hours/month if working 20 hours/week).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The national base pay range for this position within the United States, including Illinois and Colorado.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$28.40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$41.80 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks including premium healthcare, wellness expense reimbursement, paid parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Statement of Non-Discrimination: In keeping with our beliefs and goals, no employee or applicant will face discrimination or harassment based on: race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, age, gender, marital/domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability status, or veteran status. Above and beyond discrimination and harassment based on “protected categories,” we also strive to prevent other subtler forms of inappropriate behavior (i.e., stereotyping) from ever gaining a foothold in our office. Whether blatant or hidden, barriers to success have no place at DoorDash. We value a diverse workforce – people who identify as women, non-binary or gender non-conforming, LGBTQIA+, American Indian or Native Alaskan, Black or African American, Hispanic or Latinx, Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, differently-abled, caretakers and parents, and veterans are strongly encouraged to apply. Thank you to the Level Playing Field Institute for this statement of non-discrimination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and any other state or local hiring regulations, we will consider for employment any qualified applicant, including those with arrest and conviction records, in a manner consistent with the applicable regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you need any accommodations, please inform your recruiting contact upon initial connection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Applicants for Jobs Located in NYC or Remote Jobs Associated With Office in NYC Only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used Covey as part of our hiring and/or promotional process for jobs in NYC and certain features may qualify it as an AEDT in NYC. As part of the hiring and/or promotion process, we provided Covey with job requirements and candidate submitted applications. We began using Covey Scout for Inbound from August 21, 2023, through December 21, 2023.&amp;nbsp; We resumed using Covey Scout for Inbound again on June 29, 2024, and ceased using Covey Scout for Inbound on April 30, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Covey tool has been reviewed by an independent auditor. Results of the audit may be viewed here:&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&quot;&gt;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;UAS Operations Specialist&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll join Flight Operations as a pilot supporting &lt;strong&gt;commercial drone delivery under Part 135&lt;/strong&gt;. All hires complete the company’s FAA approved training, aircraft qualification, and checking requirements before serving as &lt;strong&gt;Remote Pilot in Command (RPIC)&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain required recurrent training, currency, and proficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualified pilots may be selected as a &lt;strong&gt;Flight Instructor, Ground Instructor, or Check Pilot&lt;/strong&gt; based on experience, demonstrated proficiency, and program needs. These assignments require additional qualification, evaluation, company designation, and &lt;strong&gt;FAA approval where required&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also support &lt;strong&gt;Part 107 flight testing, developmental operations, and system validation&lt;/strong&gt; as assigned, working alongside &lt;strong&gt;Flight Test and cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; within applicable FAA authorizations, operating limitations, and established safety controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a &lt;strong&gt;commercial UAS RPIC&lt;/strong&gt;, once qualified and authorized, under the direction of the Flight Operations Lead, Assistant Chief Pilot, and Chief Pilot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete required &lt;strong&gt;initial ground and flight training, aircraft-specific qualification, and knowledge and competency checks&lt;/strong&gt;, including supervised operating experience where required, before assuming assigned operational duties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain applicable &lt;strong&gt;pilot certificates, qualifications, currency, recurrent training, required checks, and medical eligibility where required&lt;/strong&gt; by the company’s operating authorizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct &lt;strong&gt;preflight planning, aircraft readiness verification, weather and airspace review, mission execution, aircraft monitoring, and post-flight activities&lt;/strong&gt; in accordance with assigned pilot responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply &lt;strong&gt;company manuals, SOPs, checklists, Operations Specifications, exemptions, waivers, and other applicable FAA authorizations&lt;/strong&gt; for the aircraft, mission, and operating framework involved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise sound &lt;strong&gt;aeronautical decision-making and risk management&lt;/strong&gt;, including delaying, discontinuing, or terminating flight activities when conditions exceed established limitations or safety controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;Part 107 operations as assigned&lt;/strong&gt;, including developmental flight testing, validation, demonstrations, and other authorized program activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with &lt;strong&gt;flight test personnel and cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; to execute approved test plans, flight test cards, procedures, and data collection objectives within the scope of assigned pilot duties to gain aircraft knowledge and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured feedback on &lt;strong&gt;aircraft behavior, system performance, pilot interfaces, procedures, and operational limitations&lt;/strong&gt; observed during commercial and test operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, verify, and document &lt;strong&gt;delivery zones, operational areas, and mission constraints&lt;/strong&gt;, and report hazards, aircraft discrepancies, abnormal conditions, and emerging risks through established channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate &lt;strong&gt;flight, training, qualification, currency, and operational records&lt;/strong&gt;, including test observations and reports required for assigned activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in &lt;strong&gt;standardization and safety reporting&lt;/strong&gt;, and contribute operational expertise to SOPs, manuals, checklists, training materials, and flight procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When selected and qualified, perform assigned &lt;strong&gt;flight instruction, ground instruction, or checking duties&lt;/strong&gt; only within the scope of the applicable designation and authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;aircraft staging, equipment preparation, site setup, recovery, repositioning, and mission coordination&lt;/strong&gt; as needed to conduct flight operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in outdoor environments involving &lt;strong&gt;extended standing, equipment handling, and varying weather conditions&lt;/strong&gt;, while adhering to company safety practices and operating limits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain &lt;strong&gt;schedule flexibility&lt;/strong&gt; for commercial operations, training, and testing, including &lt;strong&gt;day, evening, and weekend shifts&lt;/strong&gt; as required by program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the company’s &lt;strong&gt;FAA/DOT drug and alcohol testing program&lt;/strong&gt;, including pre-employment drug screening and ongoing testing as required for assigned safety-sensitive duties under &lt;strong&gt;14 CFR Part 120 and 49 CFR Part 40&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You’re Excited About This Opportunity Because You Will…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate UAS in a &lt;strong&gt;commercial Part 135 delivery operation&lt;/strong&gt; with defined pilot responsibilities and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop through a structured &lt;strong&gt;pilot training, qualification, checking, and standardization program&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply aviation fundamentals across &lt;strong&gt;commercial operations and Part 107 flight testing&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside &lt;strong&gt;flight test personnel and technical teams&lt;/strong&gt; to evaluate aircraft systems, procedures, and future capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be considered for &lt;strong&gt;instructor or check-pilot responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt; as you meet applicable qualifications and the needs of the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to &lt;strong&gt;safe, scalable, and repeatable drone delivery operations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re Excited About You Because…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Certified and Experienced:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You hold an &lt;strong&gt;FAA Remote Pilot Certificate with a small UAS rating&lt;/strong&gt;, maintain the required Part 107 aeronautical knowledge currency, and meet the additional pilot certification and eligibility requirements applicable to the company’s Part 135 operation. You have relevant commercial UAS or aviation flight experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have Strong Aviation Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You understand &lt;strong&gt;FAA regulations, airspace, weather, aircraft limitations, risk management, and aeronautical decision-making&lt;/strong&gt;, and can apply them during live operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Meet and Maintain Qualification Standards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can successfully complete required &lt;strong&gt;training, knowledge and competency evaluations, recurrent checks, and standardization requirements&lt;/strong&gt; and maintain eligibility for assigned pilot duties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Procedurally Minded:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You consistently apply &lt;strong&gt;manuals, checklists, SOPs, operating limitations, and flight test procedures&lt;/strong&gt;, and exercise sound judgment when conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Can Support Flight Testing and Technical Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can execute defined test objectives, communicate observations clearly, and work effectively with &lt;strong&gt;Flight Test and cross-functional teams&lt;/strong&gt; while maintaining pilot responsibilities and established safety controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Document with Discipline:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You maintain accurate &lt;strong&gt;flight, training, qualification, and operational records&lt;/strong&gt; and provide clear reporting that supports traceability, compliance, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re Prepared for Additional Responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You understand that &lt;strong&gt;Flight Instructor, Ground Instructor, and Check Pilot&lt;/strong&gt; assignments require role-specific qualification and authorization. Selection depends on experience, demonstrated performance, regulatory eligibility, and program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be on the &lt;strong&gt;front lines of aerial innovation&lt;/strong&gt;, directly contributing to the development, validation, and scaling of commercial drone delivery systems. This is a &lt;strong&gt;high-impact, hands-on role&lt;/strong&gt; where your aviation judgment, technical skills, and procedural discipline help define how autonomous delivery operates in the real world.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation within the pay range listed below will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, skills, prior relevant experience, and specific work location. Base salary is localized according to employee work location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash cares about you and your overall well-being. That’s why we offer a comprehensive benefits package to all regular employees, which includes a 401(k) plan with employer matching, 16 weeks of paid parental leave, wellness benefits, commuter benefits match, paid time off and paid sick leave in compliance with applicable laws (e.g. Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act). DoorDash also offers medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, disability and basic life insurance, family-forming assistance, and a mental health program, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our benefits, visit our careers page &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doordash.com/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See below for paid time off details:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For salaried roles:&lt;/strong&gt; flexible paid time off/vacation, plus 80 hours of paid sick time per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For hourly roles:&lt;/strong&gt; vacation accrued at about 1 hour for every 25.97 hours worked (e.g. about 6.7 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 3.4 hours/month if working 20 hours/week), and paid sick time accrued at 1 hour for every 30 hours worked (e.g. about 5.8 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 2.9 hours/month if working 20 hours/week).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The national base pay range for this position within the United States, including Illinois and Colorado.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$28.40&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$41.80 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks including premium healthcare, wellness expense reimbursement, paid parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Statement of Non-Discrimination: In keeping with our beliefs and goals, no employee or applicant will face discrimination or harassment based on: race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, age, gender, marital/domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability status, or veteran status. Above and beyond discrimination and harassment based on “protected categories,” we also strive to prevent other subtler forms of inappropriate behavior (i.e., stereotyping) from ever gaining a foothold in our office. Whether blatant or hidden, barriers to success have no place at DoorDash. We value a diverse workforce – people who identify as women, non-binary or gender non-conforming, LGBTQIA+, American Indian or Native Alaskan, Black or African American, Hispanic or Latinx, Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, differently-abled, caretakers and parents, and veterans are strongly encouraged to apply. Thank you to the Level Playing Field Institute for this statement of non-discrimination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and any other state or local hiring regulations, we will consider for employment any qualified applicant, including those with arrest and conviction records, in a manner consistent with the applicable regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you need any accommodations, please inform your recruiting contact upon initial connection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Applicants for Jobs Located in NYC or Remote Jobs Associated With Office in NYC Only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used Covey as part of our hiring and/or promotional process for jobs in NYC and certain features may qualify it as an AEDT in NYC. As part of the hiring and/or promotion process, we provided Covey with job requirements and candidate submitted applications. We began using Covey Scout for Inbound from August 21, 2023, through December 21, 2023.&amp;nbsp; We resumed using Covey Scout for Inbound again on June 29, 2024, and ceased using Covey Scout for Inbound on April 30, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Covey tool has been reviewed by an independent auditor. Results of the audit may be viewed here:&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&quot;&gt;https://getcovey.com/nyc-local-law-144&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at &lt;span class=&quot;_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9&quot; data-testid=&quot;smart-link-draggable-inline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;loader-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot; data-testid=&quot;hover-card-trigger-wrapper&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3&quot; href=&quot;https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-resolved-view&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66&quot; data-testid=&quot;inline-card-icon-and-title&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw&quot;&gt;Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; .&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://click.appcast.io/greenhouse-te8/a31.png?ent=34&amp;amp;e=22630&amp;amp;t=1701374353806&quot; width=&quot;1px&quot;&gt; &lt;img style=&quot;display: none; max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://track.jobadx.com/v1/i.gif?utm_pixel=224e990b-8ff4-4287-8d5d-2ff09647f181&amp;amp;utm_ptz=EST&amp;amp;utm_rqt=track&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The DoorDash Air team is bringing drone delivery to reality. To make this happen, we’re building a strong electrical team to design high reliability, high power density converters, and fault-tolerant controls electronics. Come join us to build a new class of aircrafts and deploy at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash Labs, established in 2018, serves as the innovation hub for DoorDash, focusing on developing automation and robotics solutions to enhance last-mile logistics. The team&#39;s mission is to create technologies that support and augment human networks, aiming to improve efficiency for Dashers, merchants, and consumers alike.&amp;nbsp; We’re ruthlessly focused on business impact.&amp;nbsp; We are a highly senior team composed of former pioneers from a variety of different robotics industries.&amp;nbsp; As of 2025, DoorDash has completed 10B lifetime deliveries.&amp;nbsp; We’re focused on how to do the next 10B even better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior UTM Engineer who will build core components of DoorDash Air&#39;s internal route planning and airspace deconfliction stack — the systems that decide where our aircraft can safely fly, coordinate that with other operators and airspace authorities, and keep our internal stakeholders and external systems talking to each other in terms they understand. This is a role for someone who has already lived through the full lifecycle of a distributed, interoperable, uptime-critical system in a field where getting it wrong has real consequences — aviation, finance, communications, healthcare, or similar — and wants to bring that judgment to a fast-moving aerial delivery network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and deploy interoperable services that must pass rigorous, often open-source, conformance and integration testing against external systems and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop novel path planning and airspace deconfliction algorithms that find safe, efficient routes through real-world, dynamic environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tools that help our teams and systems evaluate and optimize airspace efficiency and utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design integrations that connect the deconfliction stack to existing DoorDash systems, translating mission and airspace status into terms internal stakeholders can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with systems engineering, commercial operations, and flight operations to ship features that hold up in real-world flight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent DoorDash Air externally — engaging with peer companies, working groups, and standards bodies to improve interoperable deployments industry-wide and help shape the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re excited about you because…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of experience across the full lifecycle — design, build, deployment, and operation — of distributed systems in aviation, finance, communications, healthcare, or another field where interoperability, uptime, and (ideally) safety criticality are core drivers of the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built and shipped production services that had to interoperate with systems you didn&#39;t control, including passing external or open-source conformance/certification testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have hands-on experience with path planning, routing, or deconfliction problems in real-world, dynamic environments — or the algorithmic depth to pick this up quickly (graph search, optimization, or motion planning fundamentals).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable building evaluation and analysis tooling, not just the systems being evaluated — you like giving other teams visibility into system performance and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can design clean integrations across organizational boundaries and translate technical system state into language that commercial, operations, and non-engineering stakeholders understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate well with non-technical stakeholders and are comfortable representing your work and your company outside of it — in standards working groups, industry forums, or direct collaboration with peers at other companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong software engineering fundamentals and experience with the languages and paradigms common to safety- and uptime-critical distributed systems (e.g., C++, Python, Go, or similar, plus familiarity with real-time or fault-tolerant system design).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS/PhD in CS, EE, Aerospace, Robotics, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with airspace management, air traffic control, or UAS traffic management (UTM) concepts and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to or engaging with technical standards bodies or open-source interoperability efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with certification-aware development processes (e.g., DO-178, ARP4761) common to safety-critical aerospace software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or embedded systems, or with systems that must degrade gracefully under partial failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications for this position are accepted on an ongoing basis&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 32px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate’s starting pay will fall within the pay range listed below and is determined based on job-related factors including, but not limited to, skills, experience, qualifications, work location, and market conditions. Base salary is localized according to an employee’s work location. Ranges are market-dependent and may be modified in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, the compensation for this role includes opportunities for equity grants. Talk to your recruiter for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DoorDash cares about you and your overall well-being. That’s why we offer a comprehensive benefits package to all regular employees, which includes a 401(k) plan with employer matching, 16 weeks of paid parental leave, wellness benefits, commuter benefits match, paid time off and paid sick leave in compliance with applicable laws (e.g. Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act). DoorDash also offers medical, dental, and vision benefits, 11 paid holidays, disability and basic life insurance, family-forming assistance, and a mental health program, among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To learn more about our benefits, visit our careers page &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doordash.com/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See below for paid time off details:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For salaried roles:&lt;/strong&gt; flexible paid time off/vacation, plus 80 hours of paid sick time per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For hourly roles:&lt;/strong&gt; vacation accrued at about 1 hour for every 25.97 hours worked (e.g. about 6.7 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 3.4 hours/month if working 20 hours/week), and paid sick time accrued at 1 hour for every 30 hours worked (e.g. about 5.8 hours/month if working 40 hours/week; about 2.9 hours/month if working 20 hours/week).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The national base pay range for this position within the United States, including Illinois and Colorado.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$240,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About DoorDash&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DoorDash, our mission to empower local economies shapes how our team members move quickly, learn, and reiterate in order to make impactful decisions that display empathy for our range of users—from Dashers to merchant partners to consumers. We are a technology and logistics company that started by enabling door-to-door delivery, and we are looking for team members who can help us go from a company that is known as the place you order food to a company that people turn to for any and all goods.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;DoorDash is growing rapidly and changing constantly, which gives our team members the opportunity to share their unique perspectives, solve new challenges, and own their careers. We&#39;re committed to supporting employees’ happiness, healthiness, and overall well-being by providing comprehensive benefits and perks including premium healthcare, wellness expense reimbursement, paid parental leave and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That’s why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Statement of Non-Discrimination: In keeping with our beliefs and goals, no employee or applicant will face discrimination or harassment based on: race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion, age, gender, marital/domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability status, or veteran status. Above and beyond discrimination and harassment based on “protected categories,” we also strive to prevent other subtler forms of inappropriate behavior (i.e., stereotyping) from ever gaining a foothold in our office. Whether blatant or hidden, barriers to success have no place at DoorDash. We value a diverse workforce – people who identify as women, non-binary or gender non-conforming, LGBTQIA+, American Indian or Native Alaskan, Black or African American, Hispanic or Latinx, Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander, differently-abled, caretakers and parents, and veterans are strongly encouraged to apply. Thank you to the Level Playing Field Institute for this statement of non-discrimination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and any other state or local hiring regulations, we will consider for employment any qualified applicant, including those with arrest and conviction records, in a manner consistent with the applicable regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you need any accommodations, please inform your recruiting contact upon initial connection.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Applicants for Jobs Located in NYC or Remote Jobs Associated With Office in NYC Only&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We used Covey as part of our hiring and/or promotional process for jobs in NYC and certain features may qualify it as an AEDT in NYC. As part of the hiring and/or promotion process, we provided Covey with job requirements and candidate submitted applications. We began using Covey Scout for Inbound from August 21, 2023, through December 21, 2023.&amp;nbsp; We resumed using Covey Scout for Inbound again on June 29, 2024, and ceased using Covey Scout for Inbound on April 30, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;
